{"title":"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be real numbers. Consider the quadratic equation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />&#160;:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81c56bd71b4dc570365080882f741c47bb1ed65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos ^{2}x + b\\cos{x} + c = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Using the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, form a quadratic equation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aed45cc864c1e6b641efc3e20d277c12dbf61b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{2x}$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />, whose roots are the same as those of the original equation. Compare the equations in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aed45cc864c1e6b641efc3e20d277c12dbf61b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{2x}$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ed94ce872962a92750e1bf4b6512e4fe23848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4, b=2, c=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Multiplying the equality uniformly by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697329dcc114e955bcdcda52838505eab42529f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(a\\cos^2 x-b\\cos x+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb30eba12285aae3e768fa383522c3525485fdfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4a^2 \\cos^4 x + 2(4ac-2b^2)\\cos^2 x + 4c^2 = 0.\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"20\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce6545b53fdaa0619c14f02570204fdacab56ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos^2 x = 1+\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> and reducing we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3dc102569c1264ec2fab9fcddde4750543c00b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 \\cos^2 2x + (2a^2 + 4ac -2b^2)\\cos 2x + (a^2 + 4ac - 2b^2 + 4c^2) = 0.\\]\" width=\"514\" height=\"20\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba4ab11cae7bfdf8fd50e3307ed56a1860a4a32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4,b=2,c=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca5da5dfe8c5959a1a5feeea8f772ec74509431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 x+2\\cos x -1 =0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea391727cfd054091523de41a3bfa7ba6b89c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 2x+2\\cos 2x -1 =0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" /> which have solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436c4d00bb9b6fda071948d2124af53a3b6a55eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 72, 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> (in degree measure).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the original equation be satisfied only for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe695f9ad5226c07ffa2c67bf0521995dfc11abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}=m, \\cos{x}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"11\" />.  Then we wish to construct a quadratic with roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a6ecc35edbc60280510d1a0bf43304504de875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m^2 -1, 2n^2 -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly, the sum of the roots of this quadratic must be\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be2551379d4ee6b641ddc05f9c5d96fbb07cf0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 (m^2 + n^2) - 2 = 2 \\left(\\frac{b^2-2ac}{a^2}\\right) - 2 = \\frac{2b^2 - 4ac - 2a^2}{a^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"434\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and the product of its roots must be\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b198f599472d50216ef5529b725c649b565c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4m^2 n^2 - 2(m^2 + n^2) + 1 = \\frac{4c^2}{a^2}+\\frac{4ac - 2b^2}{a^2} + \\frac{a^2}{a^2} = \\frac{(a+2c)^2 - 2b^2}{a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"530\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Thus the following quadratic fulfils the conditions:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b365a155481d0b45acbd5b952575d8a740201764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 \\cos ^2 {2x} + (2a^2 + 4ac - 2b^2)\\cos{2x} + (a+2c)^2 - 2b^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"454\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Now, when we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d43188dd9a325642d6e64c3293387dcbce4f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4, b=2, c= -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />, our equations are \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7a9a7d05882100f4ce5eaf5e31c0357a904bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cos^2 {x} + 2 \\cos {x} - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c82dc79da7479db6fb2ee588b3f45ee0ffde9c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cos^2 {2x} + 8 \\cos {2x} - 4 = 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>This simplifies to previous equation. \nThe first root of the first equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a44202a55930e817a1bd4eb133d60368791017c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos {x} = \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{5}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" /> corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c91e62b29b2abcd5ba04aa8ee6807924e3f2b306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos {2x} = \\frac{-1 - \\sqrt{5}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" /> and the second root of the first equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3792c94bed94de3d2e9f124aa67eb2309786a159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos {x} = \\frac{-1 - \\sqrt{5}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" /> corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6aabef294678d74b4869d6230c90e2b6ffb5e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos {2x} = \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{5}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" />. These are relatively well-known trigonometric values, yielding roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6db6376ceb7f9696773c141d27b922742b97eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{72^\\circ, 144^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"117\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Text saying we have a quadratic, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1cae493c4855ca1cdd17c420fc6a97ebc082b591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> and will work with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4abb97abb9b33e74afd63fc1f5b9f38758a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=b/a,f=c/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We go from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/1654b1fa52ff96c71eb3287f61fe9c4165ec075f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/20763b3d693217a9c84a9cd0f591ae43f9f0964c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z=\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> via <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72e6f33da0c331a4a4945233f34ab828cc29cc0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=X^2=(Z+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/1847eec5ce4b18377be633b56519ccd0d1e2c247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=X^2+eX+f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> the original quadratic.\n</p><p>The opposites of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> roots satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/10881768f77eee646711bd2827481f8ed4894314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2-eX+f=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />, so the squares of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> roots are roots of the quadratic \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6965197388507d100391b752374d624cb24de692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=(Y+f)^2-e^2Y=Y^2+(2f-e^2)Y+f^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"358\" height=\"21\" /></center>\n<p>and \n</p>\n<center> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d13825f33c47ba4da67c2ddb590c7f32f78956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P)\\iff (\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />)</center>  \n<p>with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/08783b81ea64e74a644b1f74290d784f98bf183e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=((Z+1)/2)^2+(2f-e^2)(Z+1)/2+f^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"21\" />, which (through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4abb97abb9b33e74afd63fc1f5b9f38758a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=b/a,f=c/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />) answers the first question.\n</p><p>(for esthetics we can expand it to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f10c80b0980afde7af93f05dbabce933ed0cadb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^2 + (2 + 4f - 2e^2)Z + (1+2f)^2 - 2e^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" />)\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d4c0e0bd66b41d87b7eca71da7b7924cc61506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c=4,2,-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3aacde06cea2de9099481cd971bec4b668ec4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=4X^2+2X-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> and end with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a6e4551d050ee4e2d41fdbf83d5a84bda55186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, so that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> is a root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01f935e92d5237e2b29debf11c43492b27c18b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> is the other and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/724248aebaa1540e2ee7e1b867fc2f314b532cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 4x=\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> so \n</p><p>- either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62dc1151a98684cb93af634ca37c075d0e073a25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0[2\\pi/3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> but this gives cosx =-1/2 and P(-1/2)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9ddba7ceeb3ce2a7bf6491013f0848862375c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ne$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />0\n</p><p>- or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a3ca7d6c77c1a3cea5b3070e13e333b1c1300f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0[2\\pi/5]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be16a392907a6a00d553e150b453d283d083a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Then the given equation becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9a8b4c132d0aefe81eb293f92f1ccd1d28519f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a t^2 + b t + c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We use the identity\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d080ae70e351b450481c0f5973102689cf4c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x = 2\\cos^2 x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b782750b5abac1e8bceaa6b5138c2e2203ce75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 x = \\frac{\\cos 2x + 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting into the original equation,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/77773ce7eecc3ae81c37fd8cc3e7745c917e5139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\frac{\\cos 2x + 1}{2} + b\\cos x + c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a0cd7ff3f0b51da9da0607b84fc61981d7060b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(\\cos 2x + 1) + 2b\\cos x + 2c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e6482ab16c395f61bc70141e314926fa8111e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos 2x + a + 2b\\cos x + 2c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"246\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>From the original equation,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/33727661cb69aba427cf05f97505085da8c7d70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\cos x = -a\\cos^2 x - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/646e2b626826af6eefbc68dd7c2e3fbe1cd6f270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b\\cos x = -2a\\cos^2 x - 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Substitute\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1e442fdb1e3fe3dc32264018b9018f2ff1827ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b\\cos x = -a(\\cos 2x + 1) - 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d11928d05574755fd861fb7ec94ce36fd63c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos 2x + a - a(\\cos 2x + 1) - 2c + 2c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"329\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p>which simplifies to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fddc50bc56a8bb1cce603b76c8bb92809fda09c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos 2x + b\\cos 2x + (a + 2c) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the required quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01f935e92d5237e2b29debf11c43492b27c18b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c941c0c417bb1dfde5f17bc8df768bcdcb82d897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos^2 2x + b\\cos 2x + (a + 2c) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now compare the equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7ffa3b8792f0170bce1ab6008e907343100d70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a81f7c43bff36bd696d8bcde52b26bdf4a4faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Original equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4e87d600b080b28b86c1f0cfb2d5bce2430977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 x + 2\\cos x - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>New equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042bd29854e40ccf9661e446902bf32784b25dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 2x + 2\\cos 2x + (4 + 2(-1)) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d0079d4ff200545187ce9fa86a77ab40aaa1b904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 2x + 2\\cos 2x + 2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the two equations are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4e87d600b080b28b86c1f0cfb2d5bce2430977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 x + 2\\cos x - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d0079d4ff200545187ce9fa86a77ab40aaa1b904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cos^2 2x + 2\\cos 2x + 2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=~Trashboycan\" title=\"~Trashboycan\">~Trashboycan</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO\" title=\"1959 IMO\">1959 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1959 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 437/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14606/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.953      1 -total\n 42.32%    6.751      1 Template:IMO_box\n 33.82%    5.396      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3561:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163047 and revision id 284554. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}